      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I'm going to go ahead and upvote this because I had the same request and idea months ago, and I too have been hosting movie nights and various livestream events using RTMP in the Garry's Mod Cinema Gamemode for nearly 4 years now. Although, with flash being phased out perhaps it's more realistic to have HLS stream support as opposed to RTMP if it's not natively compatible with whatever internal browser VRChat uses. I don't believe VRChat still uses coherentui, but whatever it is, either of those additions, either custom RTMP or HLS streams would be phenomenal. Especially considering how easy they are to set up with them being existing modules in nginx so anyone can set one up quite easily and quickly.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
